CFD (Euler3D) Data Generator
============================

This tool generates synthetic mesh data for the CFD Euler3D benchmark.

INPUT FORMAT
------------
The CFD benchmark expects a text file with the following format:
- Line 1: Number of elements (nel)
- Lines 2 to nel+1: For each element:
  area  neighbor1 nx1 ny1 nz1  neighbor2 nx2 ny2 nz2  neighbor3 nx3 ny3 nz3  neighbor4 nx4 ny4 nz4

Where:
- area: Element area (float)
- neighbor: Adjacent element ID (1-based, -1 for boundary)
- nx, ny, nz: 3D normal vector components for each neighbor

PRESETS
-------
mini        - 12,000 elements (~0.2 MB)
small       - 48,000 elements (~0.8 MB)
medium      - 97,046 elements (~1.6 MB)
large       - 193,474 elements (~3.2 MB)
extra-large - 232,536 elements (~3.8 MB)

USAGE
-----
Generate mini dataset:
  python generate.py synthetic --out-dir mini/input --preset mini

Generate small dataset:
  python generate.py synthetic --out-dir small/input --preset small

Generate custom size:
  python generate.py synthetic --out-dir custom/input --nel 50000 --seed 123

Generate with custom filename:
  python generate.py synthetic --out-dir test/input --preset mini --output-name test.domn.012K

Overwrite existing files:
  python generate.py synthetic --out-dir mini/input --preset mini --overwrite

PARAMETERS
----------
--out-dir PATH       Output directory (created if doesn't exist)
--preset NAME        Use preset configuration (mini, small, medium, large, extra-large)
--nel INT           Number of elements (overrides preset)
--seed INT          Random seed for reproducibility (default: 42)
--output-name STR   Custom output filename
--overwrite         Allow overwriting existing files
--write-meta        Write .meta sidecar file with generation info

RUNNING THE BENCHMARK
--------------------
After generating data, run the benchmark:
  ./euler3d-cpu_gcc input_data/mini/input/fvcorr.domn.012K

OUTPUT
------
The program will output three files:
- density
- momentum
- density_energy

